			"Diverse & Tense. There is a strong divide between the vocal, legally-empowered activist community and conservative traditional/religious leaders. Windhoek hosts annual Pride events, which are legally protected but often face protests. Public sentiment is shifting among the youth, but the 2025/2026 political climate has been characterized by a 'defense of family values' narrative. For a traveler, the environment feels modern and mostly safe, but the underlying political tension is visible.",
