		continent: "africa",
		status: "red",
		legal:
			"Illegal & Escalating. In February 2026, the Senegalese Council of Ministers approved a draft bill to double the penalties for 'unnatural acts' to 10 years in prison. The 2026 legislation also introduces the crime of 'apology for homosexuality,' which criminalizes any public support or defense of LGBTQ+ rights. Article 319 remains the primary tool for arrests, and 2026 has already seen a spike in detentions based on 'intentional transmission' of HIV used as a pretext for morality policing.",
