		legal:
			"Illegal (De Facto). The legal situation depends on the territory. In the 80% controlled by Morocco, Moroccan Penal Code Article 489 applies, criminalizing same-sex acts with up to 3 years in prison. In the SADR-controlled 'Free Zone,' there is no explicit mention of homosexuality in the constitution, but authorities have historically used 'morality' and 'social disturbance' laws to detain individuals. No legal protections exist, and the 2026 UN reports highlight that human rights monitoring is severely restricted in the region.",
