			"Ultra-Conservative & Traditional. Sahrawi culture is deeply rooted in tribal traditions and Islamic values. LGBTQ+ identity is generally viewed as a foreign concept or a violation of local heritage. In 2026, there is no public community or advocacy within the territory. The social climate is one of total invisibility. Most Sahrawis live in close-knit communities where any deviation from traditional gender roles can lead to severe social ostracization or family intervention.",
